<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kampilya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kampilya was an ancient city of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabharata">Mahabharata</a> as the capital of southern Panchala and the seat of King Drupada. It is usually identified with Kampil in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farrukhabad">Farrukhabad</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a>. Kampil is also a Jain pilgrimage site, revered as the birthplace of the tirthankara Vimalanatha.</p></div>
